// @name: Sample drum pattern — polyrhythm + degrade/delay (leak test)
// @tagline: `timediv()` polyrhythm over a randomized drum sample list + fx chain — sample-set leak test
// @description: Verbatim from the official mercury-engine `examples/basic/index.html` demo patch
//   (the bundled getting-started example shipped in the npm package itself). `choose()` picks a
//   random drum name each step from `hat_808`/`kick_808`/`snare_808` (all default sample-set
//   entries, confirmed present in mercury-engine's embedded `samples.json` map), `timediv([1 1 1
//   2])` staggers the polyrhythm, and `fx(degrade …)` / `fx(delay …)` chain two Tone.js effects
//   after it. Heaviest leak test of the corpus: 3 distinct remote .wav fetches must all have
//   landed for the pattern to sound as designed; a partial load reads as a broken/missing beat,
//   not silence — harder to notice than file 05's silence.
// @language: mercury
// @outputs: audio
// @level: advanced
// @tags: mercury, ab-corpus, sample, leak-test, polyrhythm, fx, sample-set
// @source: https://github.com/tmhglnd/mercury-engine/blob/main/examples/basic/index.html
//
// A/B — mercury — Sample drum pattern (polyrhythm + fx, leak test). Original: https://github.com/tmhglnd/mercury-engine/blob/main/examples/basic/index.html
// Coller/évaluer la voix, puis comparer au rendu de l'outil original (mercury.timohoogland.com).
// Test de fuite : 3 samples distincts du jeu par défaut + polyrythme (timediv) — dégradé si chargement partiel.

@core
@tempo:110

@actor v  eval.mercury

-----
S -> v_r

v_r -> v.`list drums choose(17 [hat_808 kick_808 snare_808])
new sample drums time(1/8) gain(0.7) fx(degrade 0.7) fx(delay 3/16 5/16 0.9) timediv([1 1 1 2])`:4
